From afb9555f2e455a61d7a0ec7836a51ee775606a14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 02:29:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(stories): serve story images through the Supabase
 render CDN

Story images were loaded with a raw Image.network against the
/object/public/ storage endpoint, so every screen downloaded the
original file and rescaled it on the device: a multi-megabyte press
photo squeezed into a 76 px circle, or a small photo stretched over a
full-screen cover crop. Nothing was cached on disk either, so the same
bytes were re-fetched on every launch.

All story imagery now goes through a shared helper that rewrites the URL
to /render/image/public/ and asks for the exact pixel size the device
will paint (screen longest side x DPR, capped at 1920 for backgrounds;
square server-side crop for avatars), delivered as WebP via the Accept
header and cached on disk by cached_network_image. Transform failures
fall back to the original file, and non-Supabase URLs are left untouched.

Also improves perceived quality around the images:
- blur-up placeholder (48 px thumbnail) instead of a black frame,
- neighbouring stories are precached so swipes open on a sharp frame,
- the scrim gradient gained intermediate stops to kill the banding that
  showed over dark photos,
- a subtle 1.05 -> 1.00 zoom that ends on the native-scale frame,
- the avatar strip keeps its height with shimmer bubbles while loading
  and stays silent on error instead of printing red error text.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
