From 71b1da7c0af3adada36777fc6d848fc7d0689616 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 03:00:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(stories): topic groups, seen state, squircle
 bubbles, server-side pipeline

Follow-up to the image-quality pass, covering the rest of the story system
review.

Feed and ranking
- Groups are now topics, not articles. Every article used to be its own
  single-slide group, which is why the multi-segment progress bar always
  drew as one piece. Slides are bucketed by category (the generator now
  picks from a fixed taxonomy so the buckets actually merge), newest five
  per group.
- Ranking was is_breaking then created_at, so a 20-hour-old "breaking"
  outranked fresh news. It is now a freshness half-life plus a breaking
  bonus that itself expires, with unseen groups always first.
- Seen state is kept on the device (SharedPreferences, pruned after a
  week). The ring only ever encoded is_breaking, so a reader could not
  tell which stories they had already watched.
- The feed was fetched once and never again; expired stories stayed on
  screen and new ones never appeared. It now refreshes on app resume when
  stale and on pull-to-refresh, and expired slides are filtered client-side.
- Every limit lived in three places and disagreed (generator stopped at 10
  while printing "limit 7"; the strip showed 7 bubbles but handed the
  viewer 10). They now come from StoryRules / scripts StoryRules.

Viewer
- Slide duration scales with text length (5-7s) instead of a flat 7s.
- The timer no longer runs while the app is backgrounded.
- Opening an article closes the viewer instead of leaving it running
  behind the article, and links to the slide's own article now that a
  group spans several.
- Added a share button and story_open / story_complete /
  story_article_click / story_share analytics events.

Strip
- Bubbles are squircles: a circle reads as a person, and circular cropping
  threw away most of a landscape press photo. Thumbnails are cropped
  server-side slightly above centre so faces are not cut at the chin.
- The ring now means something: red-orange unseen breaking, green-wheat
  unseen, thin grey seen. The strip hides itself below three groups.

Generator (scripts/generate_stories.py)
- Runs hourly in CI (.github/workflows/generate_stories.yml). It could only
  ever run from a developer machine before, since it imported a hardcoded
  local path; config now comes from environment variables with that path as
  the fallback.
- Breaking stories expire in 12h rather than 24h.
- Model output is validated: a big_stat_value with no digit, or an empty
  headline, no longer reaches the screen.
- Articles whose image is narrower than 1400px are skipped, since they can
  only ever look blurry full-screen (dimensions read from the first 64KB of
  the file, no new dependency).
- Dedupe query is limited to seven days instead of scanning the whole
  table, the model gets 4000 characters instead of 1500, and datetimes are
  timezone-aware.

